        "id": 1123814
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-09-07T01:16:34Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The delay that needs to be extended is from de-asserting reset and HB I2C block being ready. The issue is that when this function returns to the caller, an i2c read is done right away. That I2C read always fails and there is no contingency for that read to fail. The way the driver is structured, I think the retimer is marked as in a bad state.\n\nWe can either increase the delay, or we can attempt the read some N times before signalling the error. I observed that the 2nd read is always successful.",
